r working with the feedback: did you use the same skill and show your reasoning? If a digit or place is uncertain, identify what would have to be regrouped or counted again. One deliberate, justified revision is more useful than writing a longer answer.","icon":"📖","notice":"Repeating the worked example cannot show transfer to new numbers. Correct the value or method, not just the appearance of the digits.","title":"Transfer to a new problem"}],"title":"Year 7, Week 34, Lesson 1: Sample spaces","unit_number":9,"unit_title":"Chance and probability","week":34,"week_in_unit":2,"word_challenges":null,"worked_example":"WORK THROUGH THIS\nExample for Sample spaces: P(even on fair die)=3/6=1/2; two-coin sample space HH,HT,TH,TT; experimental relative frequency approaches theoretical with more trials.\n\nWrite what makes this example accurate, naming the places, values or distances used.","worked_visuals":[{"alt":"Sample spaces.","caption":"Then check.","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 660 150\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fff4ea\" stroke=\"#b87445\"/><rect x=\"340\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#e8f5ed\" stroke=\"#297a61\"/><g font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#263948\"><text x=\"28\" y=\"42\">Represent</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"78\">diagram/expression</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"42\">Calculate</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"78\">careful steps</text></g></svg>"},{"alt":"Reasonableness.","caption":"Units matter.","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 660 150\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fff4ea\" stroke=\"#b87445\"/><rect x=\"340\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#e8f5ed\" stroke=\"#297a61\"/><g font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#263948\"><text x=\"28\" y=\"42\">Check</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"78\">inverse/estimate</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"42\">Explain</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"78\">why reasonable</text></g></svg>"